<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="dark"><title>LLM Memory Wiki · KoLmaf-AI</title>
<style>:root{--bg:#061011;--panel:#0b1b1d;--panel2:#0e2224;--line:#1c3a3e;--text:#d9f0ec;--muted:#71928f;--cyan:#53e5d5;--mint:#95ffd7;--amber:#ffba62;--orange:#ff7a4e;--violet:#b6a6ff}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(900px 550px at 83% -10%,rgba(83,229,213,.10),transparent 62rem),var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:14px/1.55 ui-monospace,monospace}a{color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:none}a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.app{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:24px}.hero,.card{border:1px solid var(--line);background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(14,34,36,.9),rgba(8,22,24,.92));border-radius:14px;padding:18px;margin:12px 0}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,66px);line-height:1;margin:8px 0}.k{color:var(--cyan);letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:10px}.muted{color:var(--muted)}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:10px}.pill{display:inline-block;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:4px 8px;margin:3px;color:#9fb8b5}code,pre{background:#041012;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;padding:2px 5px;overflow:auto}.system{border-top:2px solid var(--cyan)}.state{border-top:2px solid var(--mint)}.local{border-top:2px solid var(--amber)}.route{border-top:2px solid var(--violet)}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left;vertical-align:top}.ok{color:var(--mint)}.warn{color:var(--amber)}</style></head>
<body><main class="app"><section class="hero"><div class="k">KOLMAF-AI · LOCAL MEMORY PLANE</div><h1>LLM Memory Wiki</h1><p class="muted">One cross-index for system memory, current/derived state, local durable notes, and routing/index surfaces.</p><span class="pill">SYSTEM</span><span class="pill">STATE</span><span class="pill">LOCAL</span><span class="pill">VECTOR</span><span class="pill">GRAPH</span><span class="pill">Q</span><span class="pill">CLOCK</span></section>
<section class="card"><b>Core invariant</b><p>Observation, retrieval, graph proximity, Q-values, session evidence, and documentation can inform an action. They do not authorize execution. Current live state must be re-observed at the boundary that owns the action.</p></section>
<section class="grid">
<article class="card system"><div class="k">SYSTEM</div><h2>System memory</h2><p>Paths, contracts, provenance, implementation surfaces, and agent-use documentation.</p><p><a href="{{CONFIG_URI}}">.config index</a> · <a href="{{SCRIPTS_URI}}">scripts</a> · <a href="{{RELAY_URI}}">relay</a> · <a href="{{CCS_URI}}">ccs</a></p></article>
<article class="card state"><div class="k">STATE</div><h2>Derived/current state</h2><p>Refreshable runtime facts. Rendering is a projection; it must not invent missed effects.</p><p><a href="{{STATE_URI}}">state index</a> · <a href="{{SESSIONS_URI}}">session plane</a> · <a href="{{CLOCK_URI}}">nano-state clock</a></p></article>
<article class="card local"><div class="k">LOCAL</div><h2>Durable local notes</h2><p>Human/agent memory intended to survive sessions. Generated sync never overwrites hand-authored local note files.</p><p><a href="{{LOCAL_URI}}">local memory</a></p></article>
<article class="card route"><div class="k">ROUTING</div><h2>Retrieval + routing</h2><p><a href="{{CHROMA_URI}}">Chroma/vector</a> · <a href="{{LANGGRAPH_URI}}">LangGraph</a> · <a href="{{QTABLE_URI}}">Q-table</a></p><p class="muted">Indexes route attention. They are not state authority.</p></article>
</section>
<section class="card"><div class="k">CROSS INDEX</div><h2>KoLmafia working planes</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Plane</th><th>Path</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ROWS}}</tbody></table></section>
<section class="card"><div class="k">RUNTIME</div><h2>Snapshot</h2><pre>{{RUNTIME_PRE}}</pre><p>Manifest: <a href="{{MANIFEST_URI}}">manifest.json</a></p></section>
<section class="card"><div class="k">AGENT START</div><pre>1. Open this wiki.
2. Choose SYSTEM / STATE / LOCAL / routing plane.
3. Verify source/provenance and freshness.
4. Retrieve only what is necessary.
5. Re-observe live state before any external mutation.
6. Treat all indexes as evidence, never permission.</pre></section>
</main></body></html>
